  "description": "Specs: reduce tree to previous pruning points maximum of 4m.\r\nLarge Magnolia tree , 57 years old, in the small front garden of 73 Medfield Street, Roehampton SW15 4JY. The tree is in full sun; and very happy. It grows around four metres upwards each year and each year I need to prune it, to avoid living in the dark in my house all summer when it is in full leaf. My neighbours at 71 and 75 Medfield St are also affected by its height and span. It is close to the house and branches touch the roof gutter unless I cut it back. I want to prune it back again, to lessen its height and span and lessen the darkness created from its foliage all summer, in my house. For a plan of my front garden, I have submitted this before along with previous applications - look it up -it should be in your records, if kept correctly by WBC . Nothing has changed..",
